# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The disk cache for every external fetch. Git holds the OpenAlex answers and
# the fetch answers, which are a status and a byte count, because the reason
# table replays from them with no key. Git holds neither the fetched bytes nor
# the Semantic Scholar replies, which carry full abstracts.
# The extracted texts are also out, because the live run of 2026-10-09 found
# that 2 of the 5 papers that gave usable text state no license at all. The
# labelled set of day 5 commits the texts it picks, with the license checked
# one Source at a time. See docs/adr/0011 and its note of 2026-10-09.
# The rule names the contents and not the directory, because git ignores
# nothing inside a directory it already excluded.
.cache/*
!.cache/openalex-*.json
!.cache/fetch-*.json

# Editors and operating system
.DS_Store
.aider-desk/

